<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan buys Jan reformate from major at $26.80/bbl.</title>
<headline>Taiwan buys Jan reformate from major at $26.80/bbl.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has bought by tender one January cargo of unleaded reformate from a European major at around $26.80 per barrel, cost-and-freight (c-and-f) Taiwan, market sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender which closed November 25 and is valid for two days, sought 250,000 barrels of 95-octane unleaded reformate for delivery January 1-15, on a c-and-f basis to Keelung or Taichung.  </p>
<p>In its December purchases, CPC paid less than $25.50 a barrel, c-and-f Taiwan, for one 250,000 barrels of leaded reformate and slightly more than $25.50 for two 250,000 barrel-cargoes of unleaded 95-octane reformate for delivery December 16-31.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
